      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2017 American Society for Microbiology.",
        "AbstractText": "Relebactam is an important beta-lactamase inhibitor for certain aerobic organisms but alone it has no anti-anaerobic activity, with most anaerobes having MICs ≥32 μg/ml with the exception of a very few strains. There was no enhancement or antagonism of imipenem activity with the addition of relebactam, including activity against imipenem resistant strains. The relebactam-imipenem combination had excellent overall activity against the anaerobes tested."
      },
